%% Context-action double-tap request sequence
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  actor User as User pointer
  participant Surface as CanvasSurface
  participant Tools as CanvasToolPort
  participant IE as InteractionEngine
  participant Cleanup as PointerToolCleanupCoordinator
  participant ReadPort as InteractionReadPort
  participant Store as DocumentStoreKernel
  participant Spatial as SpatialKernel
  participant Geometry as GeometryPolicy
  participant Registry as InteractionRequestRegistry
  participant Resolver as CanvasCommitResolver
  participant Lease as CanvasCommitLease
  participant Requests as CanvasContextActionRequested stream
  participant Commands as CanvasCommandPort
  participant Edit as EditKernel
  participant Frame as FrameEngine
  participant Signals as Public state/effects
  participant App as Application
  participant AppUI as App-owned menu or text editor

  opt direct host-recognized handleDoubleTap
    User->>Surface: host-recognized direct double-tap on canvas
    Surface->>Tools: handleDoubleTap(position, timestampMs?)
    Tools->>IE: host position and timestamp hint
    alt non-finite position
      IE-->>Tools: reject before target resolution or request emission
      Note over IE,Signals: Invalid direct handleDoubleTap produces no context request, document mutation, selection change, preview update, repaint, or action event.
    else finite position
      IE->>Cleanup: clear pending context tap history when present
      Cleanup-->>IE: PointerCleanupOutcome(no preview, no repaint, pending tap cleared)
      IE->>IE: convert viewPosition to finite worldPosition
      IE->>Spatial: query point hit candidates at worldPosition
      Spatial-->>IE: candidates or typed non-candidate result
      alt invalid-index, stale-index, budget-exceeded, or unresolved/skipped candidate
        IE-->>Tools: reject before timestamp, request id, or stream emission
        Note over IE,Signals: Rejected target reads emit no public request. Stale-index, budget-exceeded, and unresolved/skipped candidates record bounded interaction diagnostics, while invalid-index records none.
      else candidate result
        IE->>ReadPort: resolve candidate handles to current immutable facts
        alt any candidate handle unresolved or skipped
          ReadPort-->>IE: rejected unresolved/skipped candidate read
          IE-->>Tools: reject before timestamp, request id, or stream emission
        else all candidate handles resolved
          IE->>Geometry: exact context-action hit for visible content elements
        end
        Geometry-->>IE: top visible content element or no content target
      alt current content target found
        IE->>ReadPort: read immutable current content target facts
        ReadPort->>Store: read element snapshot, boundsWorld, generation, elementRevision, CanvasElementKind, documentRevision, and controllerEpoch
        Store-->>ReadPort: current target facts
        ReadPort-->>IE: current target facts
        IE->>Registry: issue request id with content target kind and guard facts
        Registry-->>IE: issued request id
        IE->>Requests: enqueue asynchronous pending request with timestamp hint
        alt load/dispose cleanup before scheduled delivery
          IE->>Requests: suppress queued context request
          Note over IE,Signals: Suppressed queued requests produce no stream event, no timestamp cursor advancement, and no live request observable by the app.
        else delivery turn runs
          Requests->>Requests: resolve timestamp through runtime cursor
          Requests->>Signals: publish context-action request notification only
          Signals-->>App: deliver CanvasContextActionRequested
          App->>AppUI: open menu or text editor when target snapshot is CanvasTextElement
        end
      else current empty-canvas target
        IE->>Registry: issue request id with empty-canvas target kind
        Registry-->>IE: issued request id
        IE->>Requests: enqueue asynchronous pending request with timestamp hint
        alt load/dispose cleanup before scheduled delivery
          IE->>Requests: suppress queued context request
          Note over IE,Signals: Suppressed queued requests produce no stream event, no timestamp cursor advancement, and no live request observable by the app.
        else delivery turn runs
          Requests->>Requests: resolve timestamp through runtime cursor
          Requests->>Signals: publish context-action request notification only
          Signals-->>App: deliver CanvasContextActionRequested
          App->>AppUI: open app-owned empty-canvas context UI
        end
      end
      end
    end
    Note over IE,Signals: Direct handleDoubleTap is independent of pending first-tap history and has no document, selection, preview, repaint, spatial, projection, resource, or action effect.
  end

  User->>Surface: first tap on canvas
  Surface->>Tools: handlePointer(CanvasPointerInput finite down/up)
  Tools->>IE: normalized finite tap sample
  IE->>IE: admit tap if no active pointer conflict, stale token, or drag beyond tapSlop
  IE->>IE: convert viewPosition to finite worldPosition
  IE->>Spatial: query point hit candidates at worldPosition
  Spatial-->>IE: candidates or typed non-candidate result
  alt first tap target read is invalid-index, stale-index, budget-exceeded, or unresolved/skipped candidate
    IE-->>Tools: finish tap without pending context tap or request
    Note over IE,Signals: Rejected first tap stores no pending context tap. Stale-index, budget-exceeded, and unresolved/skipped candidates record bounded interaction diagnostics, while invalid-index records none.
  else candidate result
    IE->>ReadPort: resolve candidate handles to current immutable facts
    alt any candidate handle unresolved or skipped
      ReadPort-->>IE: rejected unresolved/skipped candidate read
      IE-->>Tools: finish tap without pending context tap or request
    else all candidate handles resolved
      IE->>Geometry: exact context-action hit for visible content elements
    end
    Geometry-->>IE: top visible content element or no content target

  alt first tap has content target
    IE->>ReadPort: read immutable content target facts
    ReadPort->>Store: read element snapshot, boundsWorld, generation, elementRevision, CanvasElementKind, and controllerEpoch
    Store-->>ReadPort: elementSnapshot, boundsWorld, generation, elementRevision, CanvasElementKind, and epoch
    ReadPort-->>IE: content target facts
    IE->>IE: store pending content target, generation, elementRevision, CanvasElementKind as sole target discriminator, controllerEpoch, timestamp, viewPosition, and worldPosition
    Note over IE: Pending tap state is gesture detection only. It is not document, selection, or preview state.
    opt first tap also selects content in move mode
      IE->>IE: pair same finite terminal sample with zero-area marquee selection intent
      IE->>Cleanup: selection post-commit cleanup preserving pending context tap
      Cleanup-->>IE: PointerCleanupOutcome(selection session released, pending tap preserved)
      IE-->>Signals: publish normal select-marquee action and selection state
    end
  else first tap has no content target
    IE->>IE: store pending empty-canvas target, timestamp, viewPosition, worldPosition, and controllerEpoch
    Note over IE,Signals: Background-only coverage is still an empty-canvas target. No document, revision, spatial, projection, resource, selection, preview, repaint, or action effect is produced.
  end
  end

  User->>Surface: second tap on canvas
  Surface->>Tools: handlePointer(CanvasPointerInput finite down/up)
  Tools->>IE: normalized finite tap sample
  IE->>IE: admit tap if no active pointer conflict, stale token, or drag beyond tapSlop
  IE->>IE: convert viewPosition to finite worldPosition
  IE->>Spatial: query point hit candidates at second worldPosition
  Spatial-->>IE: candidates or typed non-candidate result
  alt second tap target read is invalid-index, stale-index, budget-exceeded, or unresolved/skipped candidate
    IE->>Cleanup: typed cleanup request for pending context tap when needed
    Cleanup-->>IE: PointerCleanupOutcome(no preview, no repaint, pending tap cleared)
    IE-->>Tools: finish double-tap handling without request
    Note over IE,Signals: Rejected second tap clears pending context tap without timestamp, request id, stream event, or public effect.
  else candidate result
    IE->>ReadPort: resolve candidate handles to current immutable facts
    alt any candidate handle unresolved or skipped
      ReadPort-->>IE: rejected unresolved/skipped candidate read
      IE->>Cleanup: typed cleanup request for pending context tap when needed
      Cleanup-->>IE: PointerCleanupOutcome(no preview, no repaint, pending tap cleared)
      IE-->>Tools: finish double-tap handling without request
    else all candidate handles resolved
      IE->>Geometry: exact context-action hit for visible content elements
    end
    Geometry-->>IE: top visible content element or no content target

  alt target class changed, delay exceeded, slop exceeded, sample invalid, or controllerEpoch changed
    IE->>Cleanup: typed cleanup request for pending context tap when needed
    Cleanup-->>IE: PointerCleanupOutcome(no preview, no repaint, pending tap cleared)
    IE-->>Tools: finish tap without context request
    Note over IE,Signals: No automatic select/deselect, preview update, repaint request, CanvasActionCommitted, or edit commit occurs.
  else content target still matches same current element
    IE->>ReadPort: read current content target facts
    ReadPort->>Store: read current element snapshot, boundsWorld, generation, elementRevision, CanvasElementKind, documentRevision, and controllerEpoch
    Store-->>ReadPort: current target facts
    ReadPort-->>IE: current target facts
    IE->>IE: verify same id, generation, elementRevision, CanvasElementKind, epoch, visibility, and top-hit status
    IE->>Registry: issue request id with CanvasElementKind target guard facts
    Registry-->>IE: issued request id
    IE->>Requests: enqueue asynchronous pending request with timestamp hint
    alt load/dispose cleanup before scheduled delivery
      IE->>Requests: suppress queued context request
      Note over IE,Signals: Suppressed queued requests produce no stream event, no timestamp cursor advancement, and no live request observable by the app.
    else delivery turn runs
      Requests->>Requests: resolve timestamp through runtime cursor
      Requests->>Signals: publish context-action request notification only
      Signals-->>App: deliver CanvasContextActionRequested
      App->>AppUI: open menu or text editor when target snapshot is CanvasTextElement
    end
    Note over App,AppUI: Context menu, editor overlay, IME, focus, accessibility, text selection, hide/show policy, and lifetime belong to the application.
    Note over IE,Frame: InteractionRequestRegistry stores stale-guard facts only. It is not an app UI session and not CanvasPreviewState.
    IE->>Cleanup: typed cleanup request for successful context tap cleanup
    Cleanup-->>IE: PointerCleanupOutcome(no preview, no repaint, pending tap cleared)
    IE-->>Tools: finish double-tap handling
  else empty-canvas target still has no qualifying content target
    IE->>Registry: issue request id with empty-canvas target kind
    Registry-->>IE: issued request id
    IE->>Requests: enqueue asynchronous pending request with timestamp hint
    alt load/dispose cleanup before scheduled delivery
      IE->>Requests: suppress queued context request
      Note over IE,Signals: Suppressed queued requests produce no stream event, no timestamp cursor advancement, and no live request observable by the app.
    else delivery turn runs
      Requests->>Requests: resolve timestamp through runtime cursor
      Requests->>Signals: publish context-action request notification only
      Signals-->>App: deliver CanvasContextActionRequested
      App->>AppUI: open app-owned empty-canvas context UI
    end
    IE->>Cleanup: typed cleanup request for successful context tap cleanup
    Cleanup-->>IE: PointerCleanupOutcome(no preview, no repaint, pending tap cleared)
    IE-->>Tools: finish double-tap handling
  end
  end

  opt later application text change after app-owned editor finishes
    App->>Commands: commitTextEdit(requestId, newText)
    Commands->>Registry: read live issued request guard facts
    Registry-->>Commands: live request facts or absent
    Commands->>ReadPort: read current element generation, elementRevision, CanvasElementKind, and controllerEpoch
    ReadPort-->>Commands: current guard facts
    alt request is unknown or already consumed
      Commands-->>App: false
      Note over Commands,Signals: Unknown or already-consumed request ids are pure no-ops with no private consumption, document, revision, repaint, or action effect.
    else known live request is empty-canvas, vector/non-text, stale, missing, or kind-mismatched
      Commands->>Registry: consume and remove request facts
      Commands-->>App: false
      Note over Commands,Signals: Known rejected request consumption is private registry state only. Rejection has no public state, document, selection, preview, repaint, or action effect. documentRevision is observation-only and is not a stale guard.
    else current text equals newText
      Commands->>Registry: consume and remove request facts
      Commands-->>App: true
      Note over Commands,Signals: Accepted no-op consumes request without document revision, repaint, or action event.
    else changed text is valid
      Commands->>Edit: prepare text edit with exact before/after pair
      Edit-->>Commands: single-use prepared text install
      Commands->>Resolver: resolve CanvasTextEditCommitRequest under runtime guard
      alt CanvasCommitCancel, callback failure, or pre-install failure
        Commands->>Edit: discard prepared text install
        Note over Commands,Signals: The valid request and matching draft/session remain retryable; no state, action, or close notification occurs. A returned lease is aborted once when present.
        Commands-->>App: false
      else CanvasCommitAccept with lease
      Commands->>Edit: consume accepted install and close edit handle
      Commands->>Registry: consume and remove request facts
      alt request matches active text session
        Commands->>Commands: silently clear matching active session, suppression, and owned candidate state
        Commands->>Commands: record outer text-edit interaction revision
      else direct live request without active session
        Note over Commands,Signals: No active-session dismissal notification or interaction revision, while accepted changed text still reaches common delivery.
      end
      Commands->>Signals: outer guarded delivery: spatial, resource/release, root frame, bridge frame, final state
      Commands->>Lease: committed() under runtime guard
      Commands->>Signals: editText action, observer, then guard release
      alt request matched active text session
        Commands->>AppUI: notify active-session closure after guard release
        Note over AppUI,Signals: The listener sees accepted text and the consumed request after outer delivery. It may read state, complete a separate accepted mutation, or start another session; identity-aware cleanup preserves that new session. Flutter-reported listener errors do not stop the accepted route.
      end
      Commands-->>App: true
      end
    end
  end

  Note over IE,Signals: Forbidden during double-tap request delivery before later commitTextEdit: EditKernel commit, DraftDocument, TouchedSet, CommitPlan, atomic install, document or revision changes, spatial updates, projection/cache eviction, resource changes, preview mutation, selection mutation, CanvasActionCommitted, and engine-owned app UI.
